    ],
    "insights": [
      "The n=1 sample mean is X₀ itself (S₁/1 = (1/1)·Σ_{i<1}Xᵢ = X₀), so convergence *in* Lᵖ (which requires the sequence to lie in Lᵖ) trivially forces MemLp(X₀) — no independence, no Borel-Cantelli, unlike the deep a.s. necessity theorem.",
      "Mode-of-convergence asymmetry: Lᵖ convergence silently bundles per-term integrability (any single term constrains the common law); a.s. convergence bundles none, forcing recovery of the moment from tail asymptotics.",
      "Mathlib rename gotcha (Lean 4.26): Memℒp → MemLp; older gallery files still use Memℒp but were not rebuilt.",
      "Weak-definition variant (no per-term membership) needs mutual independence + Fubini (a non-Lᵖ summand plus an independent variable stays non-Lᵖ), which pairwise independence does NOT give."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "No single-lemma IdentDistrib Lᵖ-membership transfer used here; MemLp is current name (Memℒp deprecated in 4.26)."
    ],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Prove c = E[X₀] from Lᵖ⇒L¹ convergence + E[Sₙ/n]=E[X₀] (IdentDistrib.integral_eq). Submit to Aristotle if fiddly.",
      "Formalize the weak-definition moment necessity under mutual independence (Fubini independent-sum non-Lᵖ lemma)."
